  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic cast HfNbTaTiZr has 8–16% room-temperature tensile ductility.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic cast HfNbTaTiZr has a yield strength of 163–530 MPa at 1000 °C at strain rates of 10^-4–10^-2 s^-1.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Equiatomic cast HfNbTaTiZr has inadequate oxygen resistance because it forms non-protective oxide scales.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::chunk::001::introduction::f13797f6f6"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 5 at% Al will be added to equiatomic cast HfNbTaTiZr during melting and casting.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 5 at% Al will minimally perturb the alloy's phase balance.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al addition will promote a thin, continuous, and adherent Al2O3 surface scale.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al preferentially oxidizes because of its strong affinity for oxygen.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preferential oxidation of Al produces a thermodynamically stable, slow-growing Al2O3 barrier.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al2O3 barrier will inhibit rapid oxygen ingress and prevent pesting.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Approximately 5 at% Al will not degrade the alloy's intrinsic room-temperature ductility or high-temperature yield strength.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "After 5 hours in air at 800 °C, the Al-modified alloy will have significantly lower mass gain than untreated equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "After 5 hours in air at 800 °C, the Al-modified alloy will have better oxide-scale adherence than untreated equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified alloy will retain room-temperature tensile ductility in the range of 8–16%.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified alloy will retain a yield strength of approximately 163–530 MPa at 1000 °C.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Untreated equiatomic cast HfNbTaTiZr undergoes rapid oxidation or pesting during high-temperature air exposure.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513042::chunk::001::introduction::f13797f6f6"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is applicable to cast refractory high-entropy alloys exposed to air around 800 °C for durations on the order of hours.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Composition changes and alloying can be used to adjust high-entropy-alloy properties.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
